# What did the reasoner add that the data did not assert?
# Exercises: censo:DetectedObservation and censo:AssessedObservation, whose
# members are entailed by subsumption from the four detection statuses rather
# than stated by the pipeline.
#
# NOT "defined classes". Both were owl:equivalentClass over a union until the
# OWL 2 RL repair: a union in superclass position is outside the profile, and
# only half of that equivalence ever did any work here -- each status IS an
# assessed observation, which is a plain subclass axiom. The other half, that
# an assessed observation must be one of the four, is a completeness claim
# about a finished record, so it moved to the covering shapes in
# censo-shapes.ttl. Calling them defined classes in a paper that also claims
# conformance to the profile grammar would contradict the ontology it ships.
#
# Reported so the contribution of entailment is visible and bounded, rather
# than implied. Every other answer in this suite comes from asserted triples.

PREFIX censo: <https://w3id.org/censo/>
PREFIX rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>

SELECT ?inferred_class (COUNT(?o) AS ?members)
WHERE {
  VALUES ?inferred_class { censo:DetectedObservation censo:AssessedObservation }
  ?o a ?inferred_class .
}
GROUP BY ?inferred_class
